WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.676
Scenario: You opened a suspicious attachment on a managed laptop.

2
00:00:03.676 --> 00:00:06.985
The device is behaving unusually, and your organization has

3
00:00:06.985 --> 00:00:10.294
an incident-response number. Safest response: Option B: Immediately follow

4
00:00:10.294 --> 00:00:13.603
the organization’s incident procedure, report the event, and isolate

5
00:00:13.603 --> 00:00:16.912
the device if policy or responders direct you to.

6
00:00:16.912 --> 00:00:20.588
Prompt reporting and coordinated containment are safer than improvising remediation.

7
00:00:20.588 --> 00:00:23.897
Option A is unsafe because Public upload may disclose

8
00:00:23.897 --> 00:00:27.206
confidential information and spread malware. Option C is unsafe

9
00:00:27.206 --> 00:00:31.250
because Deleting files or logs can destroy evidence needed for investigation.

10
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:34.559
Option D is unsafe because Continuing activity or using

11
00:00:34.559 --> 00:00:37.868
unapproved tools can worsen impact or interfere with response.

12
00:00:37.868 --> 00:00:41.176
In practice: Contact the organization’s security team immediately. Follow

13
00:00:41.176 --> 00:00:44.853
their containment instructions and preserve the device and relevant details.

14
00:00:44.853 --> 00:00:48.162
Key takeaway: Report quickly and follow the incident-response plan;

15
00:00:48.162 --> 00:00:50.000
do not improvise forensic actions.
